{{- /*
  Non-secret env vars for the current user, from the single
  .chezmoidata/env.yaml (key env: {common: {...}, users: {<name>: {...}}})
  - common merged with this user's own entry under users, per-user
  winning on a key collision (confirmed: sprig's `merge $dst $src1 $src2`
  fills $dst from $src1 first, then only fills whatever $src2 has that
  isn't already set, so passing $user before $common makes $user win).

  For SECRET env vars (API keys, tokens, anything that can't be plaintext
  in this public repo) use the per-user env in the encrypted
  .chezmoisecrets/users.yaml.age instead - see modify_dot_bashrc.tmpl,
  modify_dot_profile.tmpl and dot_config/fish/modify_config.fish.tmpl,
  which merge both this and that into what actually gets exported.

  `index`, not dot-notation, throughout: dot errors on a genuinely
  missing key (e.g. a user with no entry under `users` at all) instead
  of returning nil like index does - same reason resolved-vscode-extensions
  used it (before that got folded into resolved-packages) and
  private_config.tmpl's own comment on this.

  A literal "$HOME" substring in any value is replaced with this
  machine's actual home directory before export - needed because
  .chezmoidata/*.yaml files are NOT templates (confirmed the hard way: a
  literal "{{"{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}"}}" in one comes through unrendered,
  so that syntax can't be used directly in env.yaml), and the modify_
  scripts single-quote every exported value for safety (see
  modify_dot_bashrc.tmpl) which would otherwise stop the shell from
  expanding a real $HOME itself at runtime. Resolving it here instead
  means the final dotfile just contains a plain literal path, no runtime
  expansion needed at all. `$` inside `range` is chezmoi's own convention
  for reaching the outer template context, unrelated to this
  shell-variable substitution.
*/ -}}
{{- $envData := default dict (index . "env") -}}
{{- $common := default dict (index $envData "common") -}}
{{- $allUsers := default dict (index $envData "users") -}}
{{- $user := default dict (index $allUsers .chezmoi.username) -}}
{{- $merged := merge (dict) $user $common -}}
{{- $resolved := dict -}}
{{- range $k, $v := $merged -}}
  {{- $_ := set $resolved $k ($v | replace "$HOME" $.chezmoi.homeDir) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $resolved | toJson -}}
